  "threads": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "rootCommentId": 4311494933,
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDOTXdlLc6t1Fa8",
      "path": "scripts/size_budget/fa-extension.tsv",
      "line": 36,
      "resolved": false,
      "bot": false,
      "body": "💡 **SUGGESTION: consider the vendor carve-out for future engine bumps**\n\nThese new rows (~82 MB of lock-pinned on-device AI engines) currently count as **first-party** for the `TOTAL-1P` gate, because `VENDORED_DEFAULTS` (`scripts/size_manifest.py:93`) only carves out `canvaskit/`. That is the conservative choice and this reseed is correct as-is — but it has a predictable consequence the PR notes already gesture at: every future `vendor.lock.json` engine bump ships under **versioned paths**, so each bumped engine row re-enters the manifest as a NEW line, and any single row above ~5.9 MB (5% of the new 117.9 MB first-party total — e.g. the 12.9 MB `ort-wasm-simd-threaded.wasm`) will hard-fail the daily-publish leg again and require another manual `--reseed` + PR.\n\nTwo non-blocking options:\n\n- Leave as-is (current PR): bumps stay release-blocking until consciously reseeded. Maximum teeth, recurring toil.\n- Extend the carve-out (`--vendored '(^|/)vendor/'` in the workflow gate, or add to `VENDORED_DEFAULTS`): engine churn downgrades to a `::warning`, first-party code keeps the full gate. Less toil, weaker ratchet on vendor payload.\n\nThe PR description explicitly chooses the first path (\"Future vendor-engine bumps will require the same conscious `--reseed` + commit\"), so this is a question for the maintainers rather than a change request — approving as-is."
    }
  ],
  "census": {
    "source": "graphql",
    "graphqlTotal": 1,
    "graphqlUnresolved": 1
  }
}

